# PowerPC 601 — the test programs that apply to this core, one per line.
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.  Expected outputs sit beside the
# programs in test/, where they have always been; every later core has its own
# manifest and its own test/<core>/ directory.
#
# The 601 has a manifest for the same reason the others do: so that adding a
# program written for a later core (a split IBAT/DBAT test, say, or one that
# reads the time base) does not silently join this core's suite and fail.
# Before manifests existed this list was a wildcard over test/*.S, and these
# are exactly the programs that wildcard matched.

align
alignmulti
arith
bat
branch
branchreg
bytereverse
cacheops
clcs
compare
crlogic
crmove
dabr
dcbz
dec
extctl
fparith
fpconv
fpexc
fpmadd
fpmem
fpmemx
fpscr
fpsingle
iabr
illegal
ioseg
lendian
load
logical
lscbx
mcrf
msr
muldiv
multiple
pagetable
powerarith
powerdiv
powermul
powerrotate
powershift
powershifti
powersra
reserve
rotshift
segreg
smoke
store
string
sync
syscall
trace
trap
